course: dictionary
lesson: 716
title: Bark: one word, two very different things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and bark is a good example. Read the words around it to find out which meaning is meant. «The dog barked at the postman.» Dogs make a short loud sound, so bark means that sound here. Now read «The bark of the old oak was rough and grey.» This bark is the hard outside of a tree, not a sound.
explain: Look for clues in the rest of the sentence. A dog and a postman point to a sound. An oak tree that is rough and grey points to the outside of a tree. Always swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Bark can also be a verb meaning to speak in a loud, sharp voice, like an order. «The sergeant barked an order at the team.» The phrase «his bark is worse than his bite» means he seems fierce but is not really dangerous. Context tells you which meaning you have.
fact: Bark can be a noun (a bark, barks) or a verb (bark, barks, barked, barking).
fact: A bark is the short loud sound a dog makes. To bark is to make that sound.
fact: The bark of a tree is its hard outer covering. It protects the tree from insects, weather and disease, a bit like skin.
fact: «General Sherman» is a giant sequoia with bark thick enough to survive forest fires.
exercise: «The dog barked at the postman.» What does bark mean here? | The hard outer covering of a tree | A type of bread | A small wooden boat | *A short loud sound made by a dog
exercise: «The bark of the old oak was rough and grey.» What does bark mean here? | *The hard outer covering of a tree | A sort of cake | To shout at someone | A loud sound made by a dog
exercise: Ben says, «His bark is worse than his bite.» What does this mean? | *He seems fierce, but he is not really dangerous | He always makes a loud noise when he is happy | He is a very quiet and shy person | He bites people very often
test: Which meaning fits «The sergeant barked an order at the team»? | To peel the outer layer off a tree | To lie down quietly | To make a short sound like a dog | *To say something in a loud, sharp voice
test: Which meaning fits «The tree's bark protected it from the cold»? | A short loud sound | A piece of wood for a fire | *The hard outer covering of a tree | To shout an order
exam: «General Sherman» has thick bark that survives forest fires. What is bark here? | *The hard outer covering of a tree | To speak in a sharp, loud voice | A kind of dog | A loud sound made by an animal
